# p_7a3f — Yuki cycles to work; Omar's tablet stays in the kitchen chair

Yuki commutes by bicycle on weekdays, leaving around 7:40 and returning around 17:45. Her bike lock, helmet, backpack, laptop, notebook, water bottle, jacket, and keys all leave the house with her. At the 18:00 walkthrough she has just walked in and dumped everything on the entry hook, which is why those items are there. By 19:00 she will have sorted: laptop and notebook to desk_b1, water bottle to kitchen_table_k1, jacket to entry_hook (or wardrobe), backpack to bedroom_floor_b1. Omar works 13:40–23:00 but his tablet is a home entertainment device; he leaves it in chair_k1. In the morning Omar is free and uses the kitchen table for breakfast and light tablet browsing. Weekends both sleep in, cycle together around 10:00–13:00, and run errands. What sets this hypothesis apart: Yuki's cycling gear and work laptop are OUT_OF_HOUSE on weekday mornings, and Omar's tablet never leaves the house. What would refute it: laptop_yuki sighted in the house between 8:00 and 17:00 on a weekday, or tablet_omar sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE at any time.

